&lt;&lt;orchestrates&gt;&gt;
mounts routers</panel_attributes><additional_attributes>10;490;10;410;130;410;140;60;20;60;20;10</additional_attributes></element><element><id>UMLClass</id><coordinates><x>1120</x><y>760</y><w>280</w><h>136</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>&lt;&lt;Core Domain - Enums&gt;&gt;
grade_type.py
semester_name.py
--
+ GradeType: Enum
  - NUMERIC, S, U
+ SemesterName: Enum
  - Autumn, Spring, Summer
--
Pattern: Value Object
Type-safe constants for domain logic</panel_attributes><additional_attributes></additional_attributes></element><element><id>Relation</id><coordinates><x>672</x><y>888</y><w>480</w><h>120</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>lt=&lt;.
&lt;&lt;uses&gt;&gt;</panel_attributes><additional_attributes>580;10;580;130;40;130;40;20;10;20</additional_attributes></element><element><id>UMLNote</id><coordinates><x>1480</x><y>640</y><w>280</w><h>356</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>Architecture Patterns
--
1. Layered Architecture:
   Presentation → Core → Infrastructure

2. Dependency Injection:
   FastAPI Depends() provides sessions
   Services receive Session via constructor

3. Service Layer Pattern:
   Business logic in service classes
   Controllers delegate to services

4. Repository Pattern (implicit):
   Services encapsulate data access
   No explicit repository interfaces
    Note: Repository layer optional; omitted for simplicity

5. DTO Pattern:
   Pydantic schemas separate API from ORM

6. Active Record (SQLModel):
   ORM models = DB tables

7. Factory Pattern:
   get_session() creates DB sessions

8. Clean Architecture Principles:
   - Core has no dependencies on outer layers
   - Infrastructure provides implementations
   - Presentation depends on Core
bg=yellow</panel_attributes><additional_attributes></additional_attributes></element><element><id>UMLNote</id><coordinates><x>0</x><y>0</y><w>1760</w><h>80</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>University Marks Manager - Backend Architecture
--
FastAPI application with layered architecture following clean architecture principles.
Presentation Layer (API/Web) → Core Service Layer → Infrastructure Layer (Database).
Uses dependency injection, service layer pattern, and ORM (SQLModel) for data access.
bg=#e1f5ff
fontsize=16
halign=center</panel_attributes><additional_attributes></additional_attributes></element></diagram>